                                "sense_id": "6cac9606-024a-38fd-9860-429490e78c1c",
                                "text": "The power of the spoken word has meant that some dangerous things are not mentioned by their \"real\" names, but by noa terms, like gullfot (literally \"golden foot\") for \"wolf\", or tallbjörn (literally \"pine bear\"), granoxe (literally: \"fir ox\"), trädräv (literally: \"tree fox\") or granälg (literally: \"fir elk\") for \"squirrel\"."
                            }
                        ]
